# Real-Time Multimodal IT Incident Triaging & Root-Cause Engine
Technical Documentation and Architecture Manual

## 1. Executive Summary & System Architecture

### Overview
This project implements a CPU-first incident triage engine that combines two distinct signals:

- A numerical telemetry stream for anomaly detection and severity scoring.
- A structured log analysis path for root-cause extraction and incident classification.

The system is designed for resource-constrained x86 environments, specifically an AMD Ryzen 3 class machine with 4 cores, 8 threads, and 15 GB RAM. The implementation philosophy is:

- Keep online inference lightweight.
- Use notebook environments for experimentation.
- Move reusable logic into production modules.
- Prefer calibrated tabular models and small language models over large, latency-heavy stacks.
- Enforce strict structured outputs from the log side.
- Fuse both modalities into a deterministic triage decision.

The repository now reflects that design through:

- Telemetry feature extraction and tabular modeling in [`incident_triage/telemetry.py`](C:\Users\aseem\OneDrive\Dokumen\Realtime IT incident triage ML\incident_triage\telemetry.py) and [`incident_triage/tabular_model.py`](C:\Users\aseem\OneDrive\Dokumen\Realtime IT incident triage ML\incident_triage\tabular_model.py)
- HDFS log target generation and JSON parsing in [`incident_triage/logs.py`](C:\Users\aseem\OneDrive\Dokumen\Realtime IT incident triage ML\incident_triage\logs.py)
- Fusion logic in [`incident_triage/fusion.py`](C:\Users\aseem\OneDrive\Dokumen\Realtime IT incident triage ML\incident_triage\fusion.py)
- API serving in [`incident_triage/api/main.py`](C:\Users\aseem\OneDrive\Dokumen\Realtime IT incident triage ML\incident_triage\api\main.py)

