## 4. Multimodal Fusion & Decision Logic

### Joint Scoring Formulation
The fusion layer is implemented in [`incident_triage/fusion.py`](C:\Users\aseem\OneDrive\Dokumen\Realtime IT incident triage ML\incident_triage\fusion.py).

The fusion model combines:

- Telemetry anomaly risk \( r_t \)
- Log severity score \( s_\ell \)
- Log confidence \( c_\ell \)

The severity mapping is operationalized as:

- LOW = 0.15
- INFO = 0.25
- MEDIUM = 0.50
- HIGH = 0.80
- CRITICAL = 1.00

The fusion score is:

\[
F = \text{clip}(w_t r_t + w_\ell (s_\ell c_\ell) + b, 0, 1)
\]

Where:

- \( w_t = 0.7 \)
- \( w_\ell = 0.3 \)
- \( b \) is a small synergy bonus for strong joint evidence

In the current implementation, synergy bonus is added when both telemetry and log evidence are strong.

### Triage Matrix
The score is mapped to a priority class:

- \( F \ge 0.85 \Rightarrow \) P1
- \( 0.65 \le F < 0.85 \Rightarrow \) P2
- \( F < 0.65 \Rightarrow \) P3

A practical triage matrix is:

| Telemetry Risk | Log Severity | Log Confidence | Fused Outcome |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| Low | Info | Low | P3 |
| Medium | Medium | Medium | P3 or P2 |
| High | High | High | P2 |
| Very High | Critical | High | P1 |

Routing is then determined by the priority and log domain:

- P1 routes to incident bridge
- NameSystem issues route to HDFS platform on-call
- DataNode issues route to storage on-call
- All others route to general on-call

