## 8. Weaknesses, Technical Debt & Failure Analysis

- [Direct Evidence] There is no ONNX export path, no INT8 quantization, and no AVX2-tuned runtime implementation in the repository.
- [Direct Evidence] The API route is synchronous, so it can block a Uvicorn worker during CPU-bound inference.
- [Engineering Inference] If LightGBM uses OpenMP threads, and Uvicorn is also scaled with multiple workers, thread contention can reduce throughput; the repo does not define `OMP_NUM_THREADS` or worker tuning.
- [Direct Evidence] There are no API integration tests or end-to-end train-serve smoke tests committed, only unit tests for telemetry, logs, and fusion.
- [Engineering Inference] The telemetry training/serving feature construction is not perfectly symmetric: training uses expanding history over the full series, while runtime inference depends on whatever recent buffer the caller sends.
- [Direct Evidence] `heuristic_risk()` and `extract_from_values()` depend on the caller-provided buffer length, so short buffers can weaken signal quality.
- [Direct Evidence] FFT returns `0.0` for sequences shorter than 4, which makes very small windows low-information.
- [Engineering Inference] The log heuristic rules are keyword-driven, so unfamiliar phrasing, mixed-language logs, or atypical incident text can degrade output quality.
- [Engineering Inference] The `0.85` P1 threshold is conservative; it lowers false positives but can delay escalation for medium-high incidents.
- [Direct Evidence] `ArtifactManifest` exists in [incident_triage/artifacts.py](C:\Users\aseem\OneDrive\Dokumen\Realtime IT incident triage ML\incident_triage\artifacts.py) but is not yet wired into a full artifact registry workflow.
- [Unverified Assumption] If the actual edge environment has tighter memory pressure than 15 GB after dependencies load, the SLM path may become impractical without further quantization.

