## 5. Latency & Complexity Profile

### FFT feature extraction
- [Engineering Inference] Single-window FFT complexity: \(O(W \log W)\).
- [Engineering Inference] In the training path, `build_training_frame()` computes an FFT value for every row over a sliding window in [`incident_triage/telemetry.py:62-106`](C:\Users\aseem\OneDrive\Dokumen\Realtime IT incident triage ML\incident_triage\telemetry.py:62), so total cost is roughly \(O(N \cdot W \log W)\) for a length-\(N\) series.
- [Engineering Inference] In live inference, `extract_from_values()` is \(O(W \log W)\) for the user-supplied buffer.

### LightGBM tree evaluation vs. ONNX Transformer attention
- [Direct Evidence] Current repo uses LightGBM when installed, via `LGBMClassifier` in [`incident_triage/tabular_model.py:23-34`](C:\Users\aseem\OneDrive\Dokumen\Realtime IT incident triage ML\incident_triage\tabular_model.py:23).
- [Engineering Inference] LightGBM inference is roughly \(O(T \cdot D)\), where \(T\) is number of trees and \(D\) is average depth traversed per tree.
- [Engineering Inference] A Transformer attention forward pass would be substantially more expensive, typically scaling like \(O(L^2)\) in sequence length \(L\) for attention, before optimizations.
- [Direct Evidence] The repo does not currently contain ONNX Runtime or Transformer runtime code, so that comparison is hypothetical, not operational.

### Memory allocation profile
- [Direct Evidence] Telemetry inference allocates:
  - a NumPy array
  - a pandas Series
  - a Python dict
  - a one-row pandas DataFrame
- [Direct Evidence] Log inference allocates:
  - a `LogAnalysis` Pydantic object if the log is present
- [Engineering Inference] Python GC pressure is moderate per request but can become material under burst traffic because the hot path uses pandas objects rather than pure NumPy structures.
- [Engineering Inference] The current design favors clarity and reuse over zero-allocation hot-path tuning.

